# A double that shoots for the character. GMS makes one every 50 seconds up to
# two, uses one up to block a hit worth half the character's HP, and fires five
# bullets whenever an attack lands near an enemy.
#
# Only the bullets are kept. This game doesn't value the damage reduction, and
# nothing else depends on how many doubles stand; the volley is five bullets
# either way. Without the reduction no double is ever used up, so a skill left
# on has both before any fight starts, and the 50-second wait and cap of two are
# dropped.
#
# One enemy per bullet. GMS states no mobCount and the hitbox is empty, (-20,0)
# to (0,0), so the reach rule has nothing to work with; Inhuman Speed's
# afterimage is read the same way. All five hit one target here, exact against a
# boss and an undercount when farming.
#
# GMS fires them "when using an attack skill", and the swing never pauses while
# a monster stands, so the 7.5-second re-trigger is the rate.
name: "Silhouette Mirage"
description:
  "Evades enemy attacks by moving fast enough to create illusory doubles of "
  "yourself. Illusory doubles disperse the enemy's attention to inflict "
  "damage on the enemy. Illusory doubles are unaffected by attack reflection."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 4 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
auto_mode {
  label: "Illusory Bullets"
  cast_interval_seconds: 7.5
  casts: 5
  lines: 3
  max_enemies: 1
  base { skill_pct: 8.00 }
  per_level { skill_pct: 0.30 }
}
